":"3,4,5,6,7"}},{"id":"TESTDRIVE-READING","title":"The missing wheat — part 1","subject":"English","sourceId":"SEC-1HeI7WrwumE0Q-i-EZ9-83-a6niM9GmpT-1","pages":"1,2","instructions":"Read this first part of the story. Answer each question in a complete sentence. You do not need to guess the ending.","sourceText":"\"Yesterday I put a whole new stock of wheat in the silo\nand today it was half gone!\" complained one neighbor to\nthe other. \n\"Really! Do you know that exactly the same thing\nhappened to me?\" answered his friend.\n \"Hmmm... I wonder what's going on... said the first man.\nThen after moment's thought, \"Let's spend the night out\nin the silo and see for ourselves.\" \n\"All right. I'll meet you at your silo at nine o'clock tonight.\" \nNighttime arrived. The first man packed a blanket, some\nfood and a few candles, and went to his neighbor's\nhouse. They met and made their way through the\nneighbor's property to his silo, where the wheat was\nkept. They tiptoed inside and settled down on the\nblanket in a dark corner. \nAll was still except for the blowing of the wind and the\nrustling of the leaves outside. All around, people were\nsleeping comfortably in their warm homes; but the two\nfriends huddled together in the cold, dark silo. waiting to\ncatch the wheat­ thief.\n\nAll Because of Maaser — In Our Father’s Ways Vol II, pages 119–125. By Menachem Gerlitz. Source packet: Dmai Perek 1.","media":[],"questions":[{"id":"where","label":"Where did the two men spend the night?","choices":[]},{"id":"bring","label":"What did the men bring with them?","choices":[]},{"id":"mystery","label":"What was the mystery that they were trying to solve?","choices":[]}],"visuals":[],"areas":[1,2,5,9],"approval":"approved","active":true,"version":1,"demo":true,"teacherGuide":"Physical / printed pages 1–2. First installment only. Expected: silo; blanket, food and candles; discover why wheat was disappearing / catch the thief. Do not require the later story ending. Fictiona